      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Meaning",
        "body": "A Property is a named slot on a node that holds a value. It has a name, the kind of value it expects, whether it must be filled in, and a description. What is in the slot is its value. You change the value on the Property’s card, and you change the Property itself, its name and kind, in its editor. Changing the value announces `property.changed`. Encoding: a `property` node, optionally bound to a class that defines editing and presentation.",
